{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507349-onikaze-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind-2e-conversion","id":1507349,"title":"Onikaze (Brotherhood of the Demon Wind 2e Conversion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-03T19:04:42-07:00","id":1507349,"title":"Onikaze (Brotherhood of the Demon Wind 2e Conversion)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Wave-Men, Onikaze</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Pages 157-160 of Adamantine Arrow for lore</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine and Magic</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Mastigos<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Order: </b>Adamantine Arrow<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 2, space 1, 2 dots in Weaponry, Quick Draw merit, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Athletics, Brawl, Streetwise, or Survival<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Travel to a holy place with your mentor to train with both blade and mind until you are attuned to the Demon Wind. After the initiation is complete the new Onikaze can never return to that location.<br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Time<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras: </b>Casting a spell in combat (+1); Addressing the present situation with a brief aphorism or koan (+1); Voluntarily forgoing Defense for a turn in a conflict situation (+2)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Practicing martial arts or training with a blade; Reading or writing philosophy; Defeating someone in combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Attainments</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment: Yanagi ni Kaze</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span><br /> The Demon Wind can be channeled in such a way to allow the Wave-Man to act with perfect timing. This attainment emulates \u201cPerfecting Timing\u201d (Time 1, MtAw 187) with reach for advanced duration. It takes an hour of meditation or training with a blade to activate this attainment, however, the mage does not have to sacrifice their defense while planning their action if the bonus is used on an attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Space 1</span><br /> The Demon Wind transcends both Space and Time and by attuning themselves to it the Wave-Men are capable of touching that transcendence. While activating the primary part of this attainment the mage can also activate this piece, which functions like \u201cThe Outward and Inward Eye\u201d (Space 1, MtAw 174) with reach for advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment: Tazei ni Buzei</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Time 2, 3 dots in weaponry</span><br /> As the mage\u2019s soul becomes more attuned to the Demon Wind the Benefits of touching it increase. This attainment functions like \u201cChoosing the Thread\u201d (Time 2, MtAw 187) with reach for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Space 2</span><br /> The flow of the Demon Wind is not obstructed by physical objects, neither then, are those who follow it. This attainment functions like \u201cBreak Boundary\u201d (Space 2, MtAw 174) with reach for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: Akuma no Ken</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Time 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</span><br /> At this stage of their training the Onikaze truly can ascend both Time and Space, allowing them not to just touch the transcendent nature of the Demon Wind, but to embody it. This attainment is activated during the same meditation as the other attainments and emulates \u201cAcceleration\u201d (Time 3, MtAw 188) with reach for advanced duration. It still takes one mana to activate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Space 3</span><br /> When attacking with a blade the Onikaze can allow the blade to flow along the Demon Wind, allowing them to strike at a distance. They can treat their Weaponry attacks as though they had range increments of Space dots/2x Space dots/4x Space dots. If the Onikaze has the Fast Spells merit then the attacks are treated as firearms attacks for the purposes of the target's Defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: Tazei ni Buzei</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Time 4, 4 dots in weaponry</span><br /> Those who study the Demon Wind can pull themselves into it, allowing it to carry them back into the past. This attainment functions like \u201cShifting Sands\u201d (Time 3, MtAw 189) with reach for advanced duration and to return to the beginning of the scene. This attainment also uses the \u201cTime in a Bottle\u201d (Time 4, MtAw 196) for instant casting, and therefore takes one mana to activate.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Space 4</span><br /> The Wave-Master flits from the ravages of spatial storms as easily as the temporal. With a thought and an Instant action, a space around him up to the size of a small room, or a large room at Space 5, is sealed away for 5 turns, or 10 turns at Space 5. The space becomes impermeable to all that would cross it, including light and sound, sending all that would cross one border to the edge of the opposite border. Then, he may activate Space Sight as a reflexive action even if Space is not Ruling for him, costing no Mana. This replicates the spell &quot;Ban&quot; with Reach assigned to instant casting, and a special effect.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Inochi Atte No Monodane</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Time 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span><br /> The Onikaze can see the Demon Wind and watch how it reacts to the actions of others. While meditating to activate their other attainments the mage can activate this one for two mana. It functions as \u201cPresent as Past\u201d (Time 4, MtAw 190) with reach for advanced duration and advanced scale. The \u201cTime in a Bottle\u201d (Time 4, MtAw 196) attainment from being a Time Adept also applies, making the attainment instant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Space 5</span><br /> The Onikaze may run along the Demon Wind with their entire body, emulating \u201cTeleportation\u201d (Space 4, MtAw 178) with reach for instant casting and sympathetic range, although they must use a mana to move along their sympathetic connections.\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-09-2024, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T19:07:30-07:00","id":1507351,"title":"","content":"What's up everyone. Decided to sit down and actually write up the attainments for this legacy today. Its not done, the 4th attainment still needs to be figured out but otherwise I have it all down. Big thanks to Moggle, they have already done this legacy and they shared it with me for inspiration, the final attainment for Time is taken right from them, its sick. Also thanks to Blydden for helping me setting on the starting attainment.<br /> <br /> As for the 4th attainment I <i>know</i> someone is going to say Shifting Sands but the ST that is running the game I plan to join this legacy in really doesn't like that spell so I don't plan to turn it into an attainment for this legacy<br /> <br /> I lifted the fourth optional attainment right from Moggle as I was having trouble deciding what I wanted to do wthi it after moving Teleportation to the final attainment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-15-2023, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T19:16:32-07:00","id":1507352,"title":"","content":"The second Time Attainment might need to be tweeked. I'm not sure how you'd be activating the first Time Attainment in combat, and <u>Choose the Thread</u> works better as an Instant Cast bit of divination. Right now, the Wave-man can reroll any one action, but then has to spend an hour to reactivate it to benefit again. With Instant Casting instead, they're using the &quot;momentum of battle&quot; to plan their actions out a few turns in advance, selecting the optimal course of action<br /> <br /> Instant, Self-cast <u>Temporal Stutter</u> might be interesting for the Adept Attainment, allowing them to vanish for a few turns and evolving well into <u>Teleport</u>. Especially if you add a codicil to be able to use the Sympathetic Range option for the requisite point of Mana - they go from being able to momentarily vanish, to vanishing to distant locations, to eventually just teleporting anywhere they can see.<br /> <br /> Is <u>Past As Present</u> being Aimed? I assume you can &quot;aim&quot; at yourself and have the effect center on you, but otherwise it currently needs you to be physically touching all intended targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-03-2023, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T20:00:20-07:00","id":1507358,"title":"","content":"In the third optional Attainment, I think it would be easier if the spell simply granted the same attack range bands as their current Gnosis. That makes the range much easier to manage and a lot more useful as well. Not sure about the fast spells part, though, the attack is just melee. You would probably need the <i>Gatling Assault</i> spell for that.<br /> <br /> The last optional Attainment does not seem to match the themes. Their main methodology is to use speed and reach to ensure they can cut through opponents, <i>Forge no Chains</i> doesn't build on it.<br /> <br /> Since they have mobility coveted in every way, maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1473602#post1473602\"><i>Shards of the Hourglass</i></a> would be interesting, with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced duration and inflicting aggravated damage. Mana would be spent on aggravated damage and activating <i>Time in a Bottle</i>, truncated to one per Legacy rules. Now they can make anything into a weapon that every supernatural being would have trouble dealing with, be it a crowbar, a butter knife, an umbrella or even a pencil.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T21:01:58-07:00","id":1507367,"title":"","content":"Looking back at my notes, my version\u2019s Attainments were\u2026<br /> <br /> 1. Dew of Evening<br /> Time 1 Perfect Timing<br /> Optional: Space 1 The Outward and Inward Eye<br /> <br /> 2. Choosing Death<br /> Time 2 Choose the Thread<br /> Optional: Space 2 Break Boundary<br /> <br /> 3. Chasing the Wind<br /> Time 3 Gatling Assault (homebrew spell; subject can make her melee attacks do autofire)<br /> Optional: Space 3 Long-Armed (homebrew spell; subject can make his melee attacks ranged as per the Aimed Spell rules)<br /> <br /> 4. Defying Death<br /> Time 4 Acceleration<br /> Optional: Space 4 Teleportation<br /> <br /> 5. Leading the Wind<br /> Time 4 Present as Past<br /> Optional: Space 4 Alter Direction<br /> <br /> You can still search for the rest of the write-up in this forum. And I\u2019m pretty sure other posters had their own versions too. <br /> <br /> As you can see, mine is similar to yours \u2014 but great minds think alike, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T17:08:59-07:00","id":1507440,"title":"","content":"Hey all, thanks for the feedback. Pretty burnt out today so I'm not gonna make any changes, probably will sit down and quote reply to everyone tomorrow except for Hermit, yes great minds do think alike <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T13:40:33-07:00","id":1508384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507349-onikaze-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind-2e-conversion?p=1507352#post1507352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second Time Attainment might need to be tweeked. I'm not sure how you'd be activating the first Time Attainment in combat, and <u>Choose the Thread</u> works better as an Instant Cast bit of divination. Right now, the Wave-man can reroll any one action, but then has to spend an hour to reactivate it to benefit again. With Instant Casting instead, they're using the &quot;momentum of battle&quot; to plan their actions out a few turns in advance, selecting the optimal course of action<br /> <br /> Instant, Self-cast <u>Temporal Stutter</u> might be interesting for the Adept Attainment, allowing them to vanish for a few turns and evolving well into <u>Teleport</u>. Especially if you add a codicil to be able to use the Sympathetic Range option for the requisite point of Mana - they go from being able to momentarily vanish, to vanishing to distant locations, to eventually just teleporting anywhere they can see.<br /> <br /> Is <u>Past As Present</u> being Aimed? I assume you can &quot;aim&quot; at yourself and have the effect center on you, but otherwise it currently needs you to be physically touching all intended targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, fixed<br /> <br /> Good idea, Imma add that!<br /> <br /> I'm doing a bit of hand waving and using the advanced scale reach to get around &quot;needing to touch people&quot; and having it effect the area in the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T13:41:29-07:00","id":1508385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507349-onikaze-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind-2e-conversion?p=1507358#post1507358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the third optional Attainment, I think it would be easier if the spell simply granted the same attack range bands as their current Gnosis. That makes the range much easier to manage and a lot more useful as well. Not sure about the fast spells part, though, the attack is just melee. You would probably need the <i>Gatling Assault</i> spell for that.<br /> <br /> The last optional Attainment does not seem to match the themes. Their main methodology is to use speed and reach to ensure they can cut through opponents, <i>Forge no Chains</i> doesn't build on it.<br /> <br /> Since they have mobility coveted in every way, maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1473602#post1473602\"><i>Shards of the Hourglass</i></a> would be interesting, with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced duration and inflicting aggravated damage. Mana would be spent on aggravated damage and activating <i>Time in a Bottle</i>, truncated to one per Legacy rules. Now they can make anything into a weapon that every supernatural being would have trouble dealing with, be it a crowbar, a butter knife, an umbrella or even a pencil.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I removed the Forge no Chains spell and moved Teleportation into the 5th spot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T17:35:07-07:00","id":1508683,"title":"","content":"<i>Teleportation </i>can move you to any destination within sensory range by overwriting your position (page 178 of the core book). Since it would probably be used to allow the mage to reposition to use their ranged melee, sensory range would be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> In the case of the fourth main Attainment, using <i>Temporal Stutter</i> at sensory range just means that you can remove a target from the stream of time at sensory range (although they can still Withstand with Stamina) and, since its Potency primary, it only lasts a turn. It doesn't determine where the target reappears because that requires moving across space rather than time, so it would need conjunctional Space 2 and sympathetic range to do that. It would still costs only one mana due to Legacy rules, but it requires the optional Attainment's spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T15:59:45-07:00","id":1509905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507349-onikaze-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind-2e-conversion?p=1508683#post1508683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Teleportation </i>can move you to any destination within sensory range by overwriting your position (page 178 of the core book). Since it would probably be used to allow the mage to reposition to use their ranged melee, sensory range would be unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, maybe I'll make it sympathetic range then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1507349-onikaze-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind-2e-conversion?p=1508683#post1508683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of the fourth main Attainment, using <i>Temporal Stutter</i> at sensory range just means that you can remove a target from the stream of time at sensory range (although they can still Withstand with Stamina) and, since its Potency primary, it only lasts a turn. It doesn't determine where the target reappears because that requires moving across space rather than time, so it would need conjunctional Space 2 and sympathetic range to do that. It would still costs only one mana due to Legacy rules, but it requires the optional Attainment's spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough here also, I'll make these changes later, <br /> <br /> TYVM<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T20:56:41-07:00","id":1539971,"title":"","content":"I didn't wanna make a whole new post just for one change, but I revisted this legacy a bit ago, I really hated the fourth attainment from the start (hate is a strong word) and wanted to use Shifting Sands because I think it just makes more sense, but I was planning to use this in an actual game when I knew my storyteller wouldn't allow that so I had to come up with something different, not in the game so I've fixed that, here is the old attainment though, just in case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Those who study the Demon Wind can pull themselves into it, vanishing for a moment before returning. This attainment costs one mana to activate and functions like \u201cTemporal Stutter\u201d (Time 4, MtAw 191) with reach for sympathetic range and the Time in a Bottle attainment making the casting instant. The sympathetic range is used before the activation of the attainment to determine where the mage will reappear after the attainment ends.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}